From: Ilya I. Nikitin <ilya.i.nikitin@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 23 Sep 2026 08:12:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] linking: only trust peer_id while its link object exists

si_flags.peer_id outlives the link it describes and session item ids are
reused, so prepare-link can take a stream for linked when its link is
gone. It then reports "already linked to proper target" and stops the
chain, leaving the stream unlinked with nothing to retry it. Measured on
an msm8916 phone this hit roughly one playback in 30 to 70; an earlier
form of this check gave 124 consecutive clean cycles.

Look the link up once, while peer_id is still set, and take the shortcut
only when that link object is there. Doing it once also removes the later
lookup, which ran with a nil peer_id once the stale branch had cleared it
and raised a Constraint error.

Testing whether the link is ACTIVE rather than merely present is wrong:
activation is asynchronous, so a link still coming up gets removed and
playback breaks far more often than the bug being fixed.
--- a/src/scripts/linking/prepare-link.lua
+++ b/src/scripts/linking/prepare-link.lua
@@ -33,7 +33,15 @@
 
     -- Check if item is linked to proper target, otherwise re-link
     if si_flags.peer_id then
-      if target and si_flags.peer_id == target.id then
+      -- The bookkeeping outlives the link it describes and item ids are
+      -- reused, so trust it only while that link object is really there.
+      local link = lutils.lookupLink (si_id, si_flags.peer_id)
+
+      if link == nil and target and si_flags.peer_id == target.id then
+        log:info (si, "... stale peer " .. tostring (si_flags.peer_id))
+      end
+
+      if link ~= nil and target and si_flags.peer_id == target.id then
         log:info (si, "... already linked to proper target")
 
         -- Check this also here, in case in default targets changed
@@ -46,7 +54,6 @@
         goto done
       end
 
-      local link = lutils.lookupLink (si_id, si_flags.peer_id)
       if reconnect then
         if link ~= nil then
           -- remove old link
